Density gradient centrifugation (DGC)
The DGC method is used to obtain the needed cell layers by centrifugation according to the differences in density, volume, and deformability of each cell type. The density of fNRBCs is about 1.077 to 1.130 g/mL, mature erythrocytes are approximately 1.090 to 1.110 g/mL, and leukocytes are from 1.084 to 1.088 g/mL. The diameters of fNRBCs are about 9 to 13
